export anchor WineLabelStyle:
    number: 81
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Wine label
    idea: The dashboard is an estate cellar where an engraved crest heads the page, each project is a cream wine label with its cuvée, vintage and percent complete set like strength, and status is a small seal.
    base: light
    palette:
        cellar: #efe6d2, the page
        label: #fbf6ea, labels and panels
        burgundy: #6d1424, frames, accents, this week bars and the primary button
        claret: #8b2b3b, a second accent for hover
        gilt: #a88443, inner hairlines and ornaments, never text
        ink: #2a1a17, text
        sepia: #5d4a43, captions and italics
        hairline: #cdbf9f, dotted rules
        bottleGreen: #2c5934, the On track seal
        amber: #7c5000, the At risk seal
        red: #a01d1d, the Behind seal
    type:
        Display uses Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Big Caslon, Hoefler Text,
        Garamond, Georgia. The house name is 46px caps tracked 0.3em, the
        greeting 40px italic, label names 26px, percent figures 44px with
        lining numerals and section titles 22 to 28px caps tracked 0.14em.
        Small caps labels are 11 to 12px at 600 tracked 0.24em. Text uses
        Hoefler Text, Garamond, Baskerville, Georgia at 16px, with italics
        for vintages and times.
    layout:
        A thin utility row has an underlined Seek search, Notes iii, Cellar
        master Mara Okafor and a burgundy New project button with an inset
        cream line. A centred shield crest with a B sits over BRIGHTWORK in
        wide caps and Project estate, the team cellar. Nav is centred small
        caps between burgundy rules with gilt diamonds between items and
        Home underlined. The greeting is an oval cartouche with an inner
        gilt line holding the date, Good morning, Mara in italic and Four
        tasks are overdue between diamonds. Four rounded neck collars show
        the summary numbers. The cellar is a grid of six labels, each a
        burgundy line, a cream gap and a double frame, with Cuvée and the
        team, an engraved sprig, the name, Vintage 2026 and a number, the
        percent large with complete, a ruled meter, tasks and bottled by
        the due date, and a seal. Below sit a Harvest record bar chart with
        engraved line-filled bars last week and solid burgundy this week,
        and The cellar book with italic times. At 375px labels stack and
        the cartouche becomes a rounded panel.
    spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 26px between labels and 26 to 34px inside panels.
    density: Low. Centred, symmetrical and lots of cream.
    corners: Square labels. The greeting is an oval cartouche and the summary sits on rounded neck collars.
    borders: Engraved stacks of an outer burgundy line, a cream gap and an inner gilt or double burgundy line.
    shadows: A soft 12px shadow as if labels sit on bottles.
    icons:
        Engraved sprigs, a shield crest and diamond dividers. Seals pair the
        word with a round seal holding a tick for On track, a lozenge with
        an exclamation for At risk and a square seal with a cross for
        Behind, each with a thin outer ring.
    focus: A 2px burgundy outline offset 3px with a 6px burgundy halo at 15 percent.
    tone: Courtly and calm, such as The cellar, Cuvée Design, bottled by 14 November and The cellar book.
